  "id": "nsw_planning_doc_027",
  "text": "Planning Document: Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 10 Dulwich Hill North\n\nClause 9.10.1 - heritage (heritage): The precinct contains a heritage listed water board site in Weston Street which is substantially vacant except for a small brick building. The former Waratah flour mills and associated buildings (also heritage items) along the railway line are land mark buildings within this precinct and can be seen from a number of streets.\n\nClause 9.10.1 - other (land_use_zoning): The land-use pattern of the precinct is predominantly low density residential areas with some medium density development.\n\nClause 9.10.1 - setback (development_control): Front setbacks are generally consistent within each street despite the variety of buildings styles. A setback of 2 metres to 4 metres is the most common.\n\nClause 9.10.1 - parking (development_control): In areas of the precinct where off street parking is provided it is most frequently a side drive to a hardstand/carport behind the building line.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - heritage (development_control): To protect the identified Heritage Items within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - other (land_use_zoning): To preserve the predominantly low density residential character of the precinct.\n\nClause 9.10.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): To ensure that new development considers all potential impacts to biodiversity.\n\n",
  "metadata": {
    "document_name": "Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 10 Dulwich Hill North",
    "extractions_count": 14
